According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text' [f8b7dbf88099a402]. In the input, the code fence contains JSON object A and sentence S. Since the fence holds an object, A is the scored object. In the rewritten text, the JSON object A is removed from inside the code fence, leaving only the sentence S. The fence no longer holds an object, so the rule falls back to 'the last top-level object in the text', which is the object B outside the fence. Thus the recovered object moves from {"a": 1} to {"b": 2}.